---
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import PreviewControls from '../../components/docs/PreviewControls.astro';
import BlockPreview from '../../components/docs/BlockPreview.astro';
import {CodeSnippet} from '../../components/dmf-ui/code-block';
import {blocks} from '../../data/blocks';
import catalog from '../../../contracts/catalog.json';
import HeroBlockDocumentation from '../../components/docs/HeroBlockDocumentation.astro';
import MerchantListingDocumentation from '../../components/docs/MerchantListingDocumentation.astro';
export function getStaticPaths(){return blocks.map(block=>({params:{slug:block.slug},props:{block}}));}
const {block}=Astro.props;
const record=catalog.blocks.find(b=>b.slug===block.slug)!;
const reactSignIn=block.slug==='sign-in'?catalog.react.blocks.find(b=>b.name==='SignInBlock'):undefined;
---
{block.slug==='merchant-listing'?<MerchantListingDocumentation/>:block.slug==='hero'?<HeroBlockDocumentation/>:<DocumentationLayout title={block.title} description={block.description} section="blocks" crumbs={[{name:'Blocks',href:'/blocks/'},{name:block.title}]} toc={[{id:'preview',title:'Live preview'},{id:'usage',title:'Usage'},{id:'anatomy',title:'Anatomy & API'},{id:'behavior',title:'Behavior'},{id:'compatibility',title:'Compatibility'}]}>
<h1 class="docs-block-title">{block.title}</h1><p class="docs-lead">{block.description}</p>
<section id="preview" class="docs-section"><h2>Live preview</h2><PreviewControls/><BlockPreview slug={block.slug}/></section>
<section id="usage" class="docs-section"><h2>Usage</h2><p>Import dmf-ui/styles.css in your layout and render inside a .dmf-ui scope. Supply your own real endpoint; the example destinations are host placeholders, not shipped backend routes.</p><CodeSnippet code={block.usage} language="astro" title={`${block.title}.astro`} wrap/>{reactSignIn&&<><h3>React web alpha</h3><p>Import @dmf-ui/react/styles.css once and render in a .dmf-ui scope. Native form props, onSubmit and the form ref remain host-owned. fields/footer props and children correspond to Astro extension slots. email supplies the initial/reset value; the fields remain uncontrolled. errorTitle, labels and feedback are localizable. The submit name stays stable while pendingLabel is announced separately.</p><CodeSnippet code={`import {SignInBlock} from '@dmf-ui/react';\nimport '@dmf-ui/react/styles.css';\n\n<SignInBlock id="account-sign-in" action="/account/sign-in" />`} language="tsx" title="React SignInBlock" wrap/><CodeSnippet code={reactSignIn.types[0].declaration} language="ts" title="React Props" wrap/></>}</section>
<section id="anatomy" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Anatomy and public API</h2><p>Composes {block.components.join(', ')}. The outer native form owns action, method, labels and busy state. Field, control and error ids derive from the required unique id.</p><p>Defaults come from the exported source below. Class/style and native form attributes remain available. pending disables the fieldset; disabled marks it unavailable. submitDisabled disables only submission, allowing hosts to guard enhancement readiness. Capture form values before setting pending.</p><p>SignInBlock provides fields, footer and default slots. SearchFiltersBlock provides filters and default slots. Hosts must label custom controls and avoid nested forms. Each instance needs a unique id; no internal singleton state is shared.</p><CodeSnippet code={record.declaration} language="ts" title="Public Props" wrap/><p>Source: <code>{record.source}</code>. Import from dmf-ui/blocks or the existing root barrel. The packed source includes its composed components and uses the shared stylesheet; there is no installer or second runtime.</p></section>
<section class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Authored defaults</h2><div class="docs-table-scroll"><table class="docs-options"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody>{Object.entries(record.defaults).map(([key,value])=><tr><td><code>{key}</code></td><td><code>{String(value)}</code></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section id="behavior" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Interaction, responsive layout and accessibility</h2><p>Native validation blocks invalid submissions and focuses the invalid control. Sign-in uses POST, username/current-password autocomplete, visible labels and associated host-provided field errors. It never accepts an initial password. Search uses GET, a native select and checkbox facets; reset restores authored defaults. Neither Block dispatches a request through JavaScript.</p><p>The host owns submission, validation decisions, pending transitions, results and persistence. Props describe server-rendered state; no client controller is implied. Use native events or your framework to update state. LoadingButton supplies stable action text and a separate pending announcement; host completion/error messages belong in a status/alert region.</p><p>Native forms work without JavaScript against a supplied endpoint. This documentation intercepts submission locally and disables uninitialized inspection buttons. It never logs credentials, authenticates accounts or fabricates results.</p><p>Search fields stack on narrow screens; actions wrap at natural widths. Logical spacing supports RTL, browser zoom and enlarged text. Preserve visible focus and review custom slots with keyboard input. Forced-color/reduced-motion handling comes from the composed controls.</p></section>
<section id="compatibility" class="docs-section docs-prose"><h2>Brand compatibility and limitations</h2><p>Shared semantic tokens support DMF light/dark, HUI/QDI/CB light and Portfolio light/dark/yellow. No brand colors, proprietary assets or application rules live in Block source. CB/HUI keep their owner-selected white primary labels with the documented approximately 2.57:1/4.29:1 normal-text contrast exceptions. These are not WCAG AA passes.</p><p>{block.limitations}</p><p>{reactSignIn?'SignInBlock also has a separate experimental React implementation. SearchFiltersBlock remains Astro-only.':'This Block remains Astro-only.'} Browser evidence is scoped. Earlier Safari acceptance covers the original five React families, not these Blocks. Firefox, physical-device and spoken assistive-technology acceptance for Blocks remain unverified. <a href="/docs/architecture/">Architecture and responsive conventions</a>. <a href="/docs/accessibility/">Verification boundaries</a>.</p></section>
</DocumentationLayout>}
